# Pin text sources to LF so editors, web sessions, and CI on different platforms can't
# drift the working tree into mixed CRLF/LF state.
#
# CopeTech-Edgar learned this the hard way: files imported from a CRLF source stayed CRLF
# in git's object store, and once a .gitattributes was added *afterwards* every checkout
# produced a phantom "916 lines changed" diff that no `git reset --hard` could clear —
# because the rule governs future check-ins, not blobs already stored. Adding this while
# the repo is clean (verified: zero CRLF blobs) is what keeps that from ever starting.
#
# If a phantom whole-file diff ever does appear: `git add --renormalize . && git commit`.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary types must never be normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
